WEBVTT

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.538
Anthraxic citrus
peel orange juice

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:17.573
with just a hint
of papalla seed extract...

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.107
an experimental blend.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:22.212
The success rate
of your culinary experiments

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.688
has not been high.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.624
Ensign Golwat
tried some yesterday

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.990
and she thought
it was delicious.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:31.519
In fact, she had a second glass
and she never has seconds.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.429
Ensign Golwat is Bolian.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.696
Her tongue has
a cartilaginous lining.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.863
It would protect her against
even the most corrosive acid.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:43.467
All I ask is that you
try it, Mr. Vulcan.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.483
Impressive.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.854
Ah.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.382
I'll start squeezing
that second glass.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.089
Breakfast is coming right up.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.960
Porakan eggs.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:05.965
Porakan?

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:09.524
The most flavorful eggs
in the sector.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.629
Scrambled
with a little dill weed,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.833
a touch of rengazo...

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.739
a galactic favorite.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:20.542
Now, these eggs were not easy
to prepare.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.673
After we picked them up
on Porakas IV,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.977
I had to sterilize them

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.644
in a cryostatic chamber
for three days.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.849
Then each and every one
had to be parboiled...

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.117
Mr. Neelix, I would prefer

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:34.092
not to hear the life history
of my breakfast.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:37.927
On Talax, it's a tradition
to share the history of a meal

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.693
before you begin eating.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:43.190
It's a way of enhancing
the culinary experience.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.665
My mother was brilliant.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:49.834
She could make every course,
every garnish come alive

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.003
by making it a character
in a story.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.945
My favorite was the one
about the crustacean who...

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.581
What happened?

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.089
Um, some sort of power overload.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.828
I'm afraid it decimated
your breakfast.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.491
This is what my mother

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.227
would have called
a tragic ending.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.359
Engineering has been

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.426
making adjustments
to the plasma conduits

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.404
to accommodate
a new energy source.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.930
It may have created a thermal
surge in the galley systems.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.442
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.636
Please report to the Bridge.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.668
Mr. Neelix,
I'd like you to join us as well.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:27.737
Aye, Captain.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.778
Captain's Log, Stardate 50126.4.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.652
We have detected
a gaseous anomaly

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.281
that contains sirillium...

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.986
a highly combustible
and versatile energy source.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.528
We've altered course
to investigate.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.288
Sirillium?

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.800
Yes, and possibly
large amounts of it.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.700
If so, we're going
to need to stockpile

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:51.704
as much as we can.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.706
I'd like to convert
Storage Bay 3

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.230
into a containment chamber.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.367
My pantry.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.467
I'm sorry, Neelix.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.307
You're going to have
to make other arrangements.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.370
Of course, Captain.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.905
You know,
if I injected sirillium

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.942
into my thermal array,
it might improve cooking time.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.045
Yes, and blow up half
your kitchen in the process.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.319
Sirillium is far more useful
as a warp plasma catalyst.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.825
The gas can also is used

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.794
to boost
deflector shield efficiency.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.591
The vultures are circling.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.621
Well, there's certainly
no shortage of good ideas.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.963
Have all department heads

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.968
submit proposals
for sirillium usage.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:23.969
Aye, Captain.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.833
The anomaly is
within visual range.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.601
On screen.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.600
Analysis, Mr. Kim.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.406
It's a class-17 nebula.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.209
I'm detecting standard amounts
of hydrogen and helium

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.876
and 7,000 parts per million
of sirillium.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.578
Captain, I recommend we use

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.814
the Bussard collectors
to gather the sirillium.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.879
They'll cut through that nebula
like ice cream scoops.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.892
I'm picking up a lot of
plasmatic turbulence in there.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.223
It might be a bumpy ride.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:51.958
Tuvok, can you modify
the shields to compensate?

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.562
Tuvok...

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:59.003
Are you all right, Lieutenant?

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.763
I don't know.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.606
I'm experiencing dizziness
and...

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.373
disorientation.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.380
Permission to go to Sick Bay.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.245
Granted.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.243
Deck 5.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.719
Help me!

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.329
Tuvok!

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.423
Help me, Tuvok!

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.170
Please, don't let go!

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.251
Tuvok!
Don't let me fall!

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:00.464
No!

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:05.420
I was holding a young girl
by the hand,

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:08.256
trying to prevent her
from falling from a precipice.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:12.822
I was unable to keep my grip,
and she fell to her death.

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:15.333
And there is more.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.598
I had an emotional response...

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:20.367
anxiety, fear...

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:22.567
an almost irrational
anger at myself

00:07:22.609 --> 00:07:23.633
for letting her fall.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.303
When did that happen?

00:07:25.345 --> 00:07:27.074
It never happened.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.343
The girl was unfamiliar

00:07:29.382 --> 00:07:31.213
and I've never been
in that situation.

00:07:31.251 --> 00:07:36.746
It was me as a child
and it did seem like a memory,

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:39.155
but I don't recall the incident.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:41.683
Well, it was definitely
a traumatic episode.

00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:45.129
Your heart rate accelerated
to 300 beats per minute

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:48.292
your adrenaline levels
rose by 113 percent

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.325
and your neuroelectrical
readings

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.133
nearly jumped off the scale.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:54.731
If you were human, I'd say
you had a severe panic attack.

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:55.934
I am not human.

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:57.203
No kidding.

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:59.234
I don't know
what happened to you,

00:07:59.279 --> 00:08:01.611
but there can be any number
of explanations...

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:05.084
hallucination, telepathic
communication from another race,

00:08:05.118 --> 00:08:06.517
repressed memory,

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:08.918
momentary contact
with a parallel reality.

00:08:08.955 --> 00:08:09.922
Take your pick.

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:12.014
The universe is
such a strange place.

00:08:12.058 --> 00:08:14.356
I'll have Mr. Kim
examine the sensor logs.

00:08:14.394 --> 00:08:16.021
Maybe our proximity
to the nebula

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.529
is affecting you somehow.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:20.623
In the meantime, Lieutenant,
you are free to go.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:22.294
All of your vital signs
have returned to normal

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:24.735
and I don't see
any residual systemic damage.

00:08:24.771 --> 00:08:29.333
But I want you to wear
this neurocortical monitor.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.036
In case you have
another episode,

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:34.444
it'll record a complete
encephalographic profile

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.414
and alert Sick Bay
at the same time.

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:37.939
A wise precaution, Doctor.

00:08:38.051 --> 00:08:39.109
Thank you.

00:08:47.694 --> 00:08:49.753
Structure.

00:08:49.796 --> 00:08:51.423
Logic.

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:53.489
Function.

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.160
Control.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:58.967
A structure cannot stand
without a foundation.

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:02.873
Logic is the foundation
of function.

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:05.070
Function...

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:08.205
is the essence of control.

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:11.944
I am in control.

00:09:14.087 --> 00:09:16.954
I am in control.

00:09:25.031 --> 00:09:26.020
Enter.

00:09:28.101 --> 00:09:29.830
Kes.

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:32.495
What is it?

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:33.937
The Doctor wanted
me to adjust your

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.271
neurocortical monitor to pick
up additional peptide readings.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.939
I can come back later
if this is a bad time.

00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:42.742
No.

00:09:42.782 --> 00:09:44.306
You may proceed.

00:09:49.489 --> 00:09:51.047
What are you working on?

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.955
It is called a keethara.

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.686
Keethara?

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:56.524
What does that mean?

00:09:57.764 --> 00:10:01.222
The approximate translation
is "structure of harmony."

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:04.464
It is used as a mediational aid.

00:10:04.504 --> 00:10:07.803
Building it
requires precise balance

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.603
and spatial acuity.

00:10:09.642 --> 00:10:14.011
It helps to focus thought
and refine mental control.

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:18.247
At the moment, it doesn't
look very harmonious.

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.516
No. It does not.

00:10:23.656 --> 00:10:25.556
I'm curious.

00:10:25.591 --> 00:10:28.321
What does a keethara
look like when it's done?

00:10:28.361 --> 00:10:30.420
The form is not predefined.

00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:33.762
It is a reflection
of the builder's state of mind.

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.236
Thus, it is different each time.

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:39.636
I'd like to see it
when it's finished.

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:45.840
Well, good night.

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:48.905
Kes...

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.015
It's all right.

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:55.212
I understand.

00:11:02.595 --> 00:11:04.825
Structure.

00:11:04.864 --> 00:11:06.832
Logic.

00:11:06.866 --> 00:11:08.891
Function.

00:11:08.935 --> 00:11:11.233
Control.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:14.433
A structure cannot stand

00:11:14.474 --> 00:11:16.874
without a foundation.

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:20.345
Logic is the foundation...

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:22.904
of function.

00:11:22.949 --> 00:11:26.407
Function is the essence
of control.

00:11:27.854 --> 00:11:30.448
I am in control.

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:35.092
I am in...

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:36.719
control.

00:11:36.762 --> 00:11:38.093
So how are you feeling
this morning?

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.995
If you are referring
to yesterday's incident,

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:42.260
I haven't experienced
any further problems.

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:43.632
I am fit for duty.

00:11:43.669 --> 00:11:45.296
I didn't ask
because I'm concerned

00:11:45.338 --> 00:11:46.669
about your ability to perform.

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:47.798
I'm concerned about you.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.467
There is no need for concern.

00:11:49.509 --> 00:11:51.636
Sorry I asked.

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:54.879
My apologies, Commander.

00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:56.609
I am distracted.

00:11:56.649 --> 00:11:58.480
I spent 14 hours last night

00:11:58.518 --> 00:12:00.577
in deep meditation
trying to determine

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.588
the source
of my aberrant behavior.

00:12:02.622 --> 00:12:03.953
I could not.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.821
Maybe you should try to forget
about it for a while.

00:12:05.858 --> 00:12:08.088
I've found that when you
don't think about a problem,

00:12:08.127 --> 00:12:09.685
sometimes the solution
comes to you.

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:11.094
It is difficult to forget

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:12.961
when you're wearing
a neurocortical monitor

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.362
on your parietal bone.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.561
Good point.
Mr. Kim?

00:12:16.602 --> 00:12:18.866
I checked all the sensor logs.

00:12:18.905 --> 00:12:21.499
There's no sign of anything
emanating from the nebula

00:12:21.541 --> 00:12:23.668
that would have
affected Tuvok or Voyager.

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:25.973
Anything unusual
about the nebula itself?

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:28.603
No. It's a standard class-17.

00:12:28.648 --> 00:12:31.879
I suggest we conduct
a tachyon sweep of the nebula.

00:12:31.918 --> 00:12:34.216
It would reveal the presence
of any cloaked ships.

00:12:34.253 --> 00:12:36.949
Cloaked ships?

00:12:36.989 --> 00:12:39.219
Yes. We should be
extremely cautious

00:12:39.258 --> 00:12:41.158
this close to Klingon space.

00:12:41.193 --> 00:12:43.354
Tuvok, the Klingon Empire

00:12:43.396 --> 00:12:45.330
is on the other side
of the galaxy.

00:12:47.233 --> 00:12:50.862
Yes. Yes, you are right,
of course.

00:12:50.903 --> 00:12:55.135
I'm uncertain why I would
make such an obvious error.

00:12:55.174 --> 00:12:57.108
Maybe you should go
back to Sick Bay.

00:13:01.113 --> 00:13:02.876
Tuvok?

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:03.904
Help me, Tuvok!

00:13:04.417 --> 00:13:05.782
Please, don't let go!

00:13:06.419 --> 00:13:07.784
No!

00:13:27.239 --> 00:13:29.969
I think we may be dealing
with a repressed memory.

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:31.805
The memory engrams
in the dorsal region

00:13:31.844 --> 00:13:34.210
of the hippocampus
are being disrupted.

00:13:34.246 --> 00:13:37.374
It's causing physical damage
to the surrounding tissue.

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:40.510
In Vulcan medicine,
this is known as t'Iokan schism.

00:13:40.553 --> 00:13:43.545
It means that the subject is
inhibiting a traumatic memory,

00:13:43.589 --> 00:13:45.750
which is beginning to resurface.

00:13:45.791 --> 00:13:47.656
And that's causing brain damage?

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:49.160
Strange, I know.

00:13:49.195 --> 00:13:50.992
In human subjects,
repressed memories

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.498
are nothing more than
psychological traumas,

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:54.760
which can be dealt
with with standard

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.700
therapeutic techniques,
but in Vulcans,

00:13:56.736 --> 00:13:59.398
there is a physical reaction
to the battle between

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:00.700
the conscious
and the unconscious.

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.765
In extreme cases,
the mind of the patient

00:14:02.808 --> 00:14:05.368
can literally...
Iobotomize itself.

00:14:05.411 --> 00:14:06.571
What's the treatment?

00:14:06.612 --> 00:14:09.547
There is no medical treatment
for this condition.

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:12.210
Vulcan psychocognitive
research suggests

00:14:12.251 --> 00:14:15.186
that the patient initiate a
mind-meld with a family member

00:14:15.221 --> 00:14:16.950
and the two of them
attempt to bring

00:14:16.989 --> 00:14:20.117
the repressed memory
into the conscious mind.

00:14:20.159 --> 00:14:21.217
I'm the closest thing

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.455
Tuvok has to a family
member on this ship.

00:14:23.496 --> 00:14:25.123
That's why I've
asked you to come.

00:14:25.164 --> 00:14:26.529
He has a request to make of you.

00:14:31.971 --> 00:14:34.235
Did the Doctor explain
the situation to you?

00:14:34.273 --> 00:14:35.604
Yes.

00:14:35.641 --> 00:14:38.906
Tuvok, are you sure it's
the right thing to do?

00:14:38.944 --> 00:14:41.708
I don't know
how else to proceed.

00:14:41.747 --> 00:14:44.910
The Doctor tells me
that this is a memory.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:49.387
And yet, no matter how hard
I try, I cannot remember.

00:14:51.157 --> 00:14:54.092
If the Doctor is correct,
if this is an experience

00:14:54.126 --> 00:14:56.856
I pushed
into my unconscious mind,

00:14:56.896 --> 00:15:01.924
it could be very dangerous
to me, even life-threatening.

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:06.529
I realize it's asking
a great deal of you, Captain,

00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:10.235
and I did consider turning to
one of the Vulcans on the ship,

00:15:10.276 --> 00:15:13.939
but this meld would be
more intimate than most.

00:15:13.979 --> 00:15:16.641
A family member
is normally chosen

00:15:16.682 --> 00:15:20.448
because of the implicit trust
that usually exists.

00:15:20.486 --> 00:15:23.046
On this ship...

00:15:23.089 --> 00:15:25.557
I trust you
more than anyone else.

00:15:29.228 --> 00:15:33.255
Whatever happens,
I'll be there for you, Tuvok.

00:15:33.299 --> 00:15:35.096
I'll help you get through this.

00:15:37.203 --> 00:15:38.636
I will initiate the meld

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:42.266
and attempt to access
the memory fragment.

00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:45.811
Once that has been accomplished,
you will act as my pyllora.

00:15:45.944 --> 00:15:47.536
Your pyllora.

00:15:47.579 --> 00:15:50.480
My guide.
My counselor.

00:15:50.515 --> 00:15:52.983
You will help me reconstruct
the memory in its entirety.

00:15:53.018 --> 00:15:54.508
And as I am reliving it,

00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:57.351
you will help me to objectify
the experience.

00:15:57.389 --> 00:16:00.916
By processing the experience
rather than repressing it,

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:04.224
I can begin to overcome
my fear, anger

00:16:04.262 --> 00:16:05.729
and the other
emotional responses

00:16:05.764 --> 00:16:09.427
and to reintegrate the memory
into my conscious mind.

00:16:09.467 --> 00:16:11.059
When I'm in your memory,

00:16:11.102 --> 00:16:13.696
will I actually be
reliving it with you?

00:16:13.738 --> 00:16:15.137
No.

00:16:15.173 --> 00:16:17.505
I will be the only one
who notices your presence.

00:16:17.542 --> 00:16:19.942
You will be an observer
in the memory

00:16:20.011 --> 00:16:21.638
but not a participant.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.774
This will give you the freedom
to guide me objectively.

00:16:27.853 --> 00:16:29.150
When do we start?

00:16:30.155 --> 00:16:32.180
I will need time to prepare.

00:16:32.224 --> 00:16:34.283
Please return in one hour.

00:16:47.739 --> 00:16:49.570
We're ready when you are,
Captain.

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:59.176
Your mind to my mind.

00:16:59.217 --> 00:17:03.449
Your thoughts...
to my thoughts.

00:17:03.488 --> 00:17:06.423
I am taking us back...

00:17:06.458 --> 00:17:09.621
back to the boy that I was...

00:17:09.661 --> 00:17:12.459
the boy lying on the precipice.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:15.924
Return fire!

00:17:16.034 --> 00:17:17.729
They've knocked out
our targeting scanners.

00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:21.098
Mr. Valtane...

00:17:23.475 --> 00:17:24.874
Get away from that station!

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:25.467
One more second.

00:17:26.311 --> 00:17:27.642
Damage report!

00:17:32.918 --> 00:17:33.942
Seal that conduit!

00:17:34.052 --> 00:17:36.953
Hull breach on Deck 12,
Section 47.

00:17:36.988 --> 00:17:39.388
We've lost power
on Decks 5, 6 and 10.

00:17:39.424 --> 00:17:40.914
Casualty reports coming in.

00:17:40.959 --> 00:17:42.119
19 wounded.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.787
Tuvok, can you see me?

00:17:43.828 --> 00:17:44.795
Yes.

00:17:44.829 --> 00:17:46.057
Where are we?

00:17:46.097 --> 00:17:48.463
My first deep space assignment
aboard the Excelsior.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.489
Why did you bring us here?

00:17:49.534 --> 00:17:50.899
I did not intend to.

00:17:50.936 --> 00:17:53.336
Can you take us to the
precipice? The girl?

00:17:53.371 --> 00:17:55.737
That is precisely
what I attempted to do.

00:17:55.774 --> 00:17:58.834
There must be some reason
why your mind brought us here.

00:17:58.877 --> 00:18:01.744
Maybe this memory is connected
to the girl in some way.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:03.077
How along ago is this?

00:18:03.114 --> 00:18:05.378
Stardate 9521.

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:06.816
Approximately 80 years ago.

00:18:06.851 --> 00:18:08.478
Who are you fighting?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:09.714
The Klingons.

00:18:09.754 --> 00:18:10.914
Klingons?

00:18:10.956 --> 00:18:12.685
Before you collapsed
in Engineering,

00:18:12.724 --> 00:18:14.783
you thought we were
approaching Klingon space.

00:18:16.094 --> 00:18:17.925
Why are you fighting
the Klingons?

00:18:18.029 --> 00:18:19.291
This battle was precipitated

00:18:19.331 --> 00:18:21.663
by an incident that took
place three days earlier.

00:18:22.934 --> 00:18:24.561
All right, Gamma Shift

00:18:24.602 --> 00:18:27.503
time to defend the Federation
against gaseous anomalies.

00:18:27.539 --> 00:18:29.530
Gaseous anomalies?

00:18:29.574 --> 00:18:32.065
We were charting
a gaseous anomaly on Voyager.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.771
And that's
when my problem began.

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:35.370
That's more than a coincidence.

00:18:35.413 --> 00:18:36.710
How are you this morning,
Ensign?

00:18:36.748 --> 00:18:38.306
I am well, Commander.
Thank you.

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:39.578
I thought you might like to see

00:18:39.617 --> 00:18:41.244
some of this morning's
com traffic

00:18:41.286 --> 00:18:42.719
before you went on duty.

00:18:42.754 --> 00:18:44.551
There's a message
from the Yorktown

00:18:44.589 --> 00:18:46.352
I think you might
be interested in.

00:18:46.391 --> 00:18:47.915
It's from your father.

00:18:47.959 --> 00:18:48.948
Thank you.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:51.722
You're not going to have
time to drink that, you know.

00:18:51.763 --> 00:18:53.958
You're due on the
Bridge in five minutes.

00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:56.398
It's not for me.
It's for the Captain.

00:18:56.434 --> 00:18:57.867
I've observed that Captain Sulu

00:18:57.902 --> 00:18:59.597
drinks a cup of tea
each morning.

00:18:59.637 --> 00:19:01.571
I thought he might enjoy
a Vulcan blend.

00:19:01.606 --> 00:19:03.130
Oh, I see.

00:19:03.174 --> 00:19:05.642
Trying to make Lieutenant
in your first month?

00:19:05.677 --> 00:19:08.840
I wish I'd have thought of that
when I was your age.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:11.348
Took me three years
just to make Ensign.

00:19:11.383 --> 00:19:13.510
I assure you I have
no ulterior motive.

00:19:13.551 --> 00:19:15.883
Whatever you say, Ensign.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.114
See you on the Bridge.

00:19:19.224 --> 00:19:20.919
You've never brought me tea.

00:19:31.636 --> 00:19:33.035
Outstanding.

00:19:33.071 --> 00:19:35.164
I may have to give
you a promotion.

00:19:35.206 --> 00:19:37.231
That was not my motivation,
Captain.

00:19:37.275 --> 00:19:40.267
I am not attempting to curry
favor with you in any way.

00:19:40.311 --> 00:19:43.712
Mr. Tuvok, if you're going
to remain on my ship,

00:19:43.748 --> 00:19:46.911
you're going to have to learn
how to appreciate a joke.

00:19:46.951 --> 00:19:49.852
And don't tell me Vulcans
don't have a sense of humor

00:19:49.888 --> 00:19:51.879
because I know better.

00:19:51.923 --> 00:19:55.154
I will... work on it, sir.

00:19:55.193 --> 00:19:57.855
Very good.
And... thanks again.

00:20:00.965 --> 00:20:03.399
He doesn't look anything
like his portrait

00:20:03.435 --> 00:20:04.561
at Starfleet Headquarters.

00:20:04.602 --> 00:20:06.160
In the 23rd century,

00:20:06.204 --> 00:20:09.196
holographic imaging resolution
was less accurate.

00:20:10.642 --> 00:20:12.610
This is a science station,
isn't it?

00:20:12.644 --> 00:20:15.477
Yes. I am one of several
junior science officers.

00:20:15.513 --> 00:20:19.347
Tuvok, why doesn't your service
record reflect any of this?

00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:21.978
I thought your first assignment
was aboard the Wyoming.

00:20:22.087 --> 00:20:24.715
It's a long story, Captain,
but suffice it to say,

00:20:24.756 --> 00:20:26.951
this was
my first Starfleet career.

00:20:26.991 --> 00:20:28.652
I was 29 years old.

00:20:28.693 --> 00:20:30.217
So, what's happening?

00:20:30.261 --> 00:20:31.922
Are we about to encounter
the Klingons?

00:20:31.963 --> 00:20:32.987
Not exactly.

00:20:33.098 --> 00:20:35.191
The Klingon moon Praxis
is about to explode.

00:20:35.233 --> 00:20:36.359
Praxis.

00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:38.494
During this period, it was
a primary source of energy

00:20:38.536 --> 00:20:39.594
for the Klingon Homeworld.

00:20:39.637 --> 00:20:42.162
Praxis... yes.

00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:44.402
Its destruction would
have lasting repercussions

00:20:44.442 --> 00:20:47.104
throughout the Quadrant,
and it led to the first

00:20:47.145 --> 00:20:48.976
Federation-Klingon peace treaty.

00:20:49.013 --> 00:20:49.980
That is correct.

00:20:50.014 --> 00:20:51.413
But what does
all this have to do

00:20:51.449 --> 00:20:52.848
with the girl on the precipice?

00:21:04.963 --> 00:21:07.659
I have an energy wave at 240
degrees, mark 6 port, sir.

00:21:07.699 --> 00:21:08.961
Visual.

00:21:10.034 --> 00:21:12.594
My... God!

00:21:16.474 --> 00:21:18.465
Shields! Shields!

00:21:26.451 --> 00:21:29.113
She is not answering the helm.

00:21:29.154 --> 00:21:30.121
Starboard thrusters.

00:21:30.155 --> 00:21:31.122
Turn her into the wave.

00:21:31.156 --> 00:21:32.555
Aye, sir.

00:21:36.594 --> 00:21:37.925
Quarter impulse power.

00:21:37.962 --> 00:21:40.123
Damage report.

00:21:40.165 --> 00:21:41.996
Checking all systems, Captain.

00:21:48.706 --> 00:21:51.573
Don't tell me
that was any meteor shower.

00:21:51.609 --> 00:21:53.008
Negative, sir.

00:21:53.111 --> 00:21:54.135
The subspace shock wave

00:21:54.179 --> 00:21:57.342
originated
at bearing 323 mark 75.

00:21:57.382 --> 00:21:58.974
Location...

00:21:59.017 --> 00:22:00.143
It's Praxis, sir.

00:22:00.185 --> 00:22:01.243
It's a Klingon moon.

00:22:01.286 --> 00:22:05.518
Praxis is their key
energy production facility.

00:22:05.557 --> 00:22:07.821
So, what happened?
Did you go to Praxis?

00:22:07.859 --> 00:22:10.157
No. We were warned off
by the Klingons

00:22:10.195 --> 00:22:11.958
and resumed our survey mission.

00:22:11.996 --> 00:22:13.156
However, two days later,

00:22:13.198 --> 00:22:15.098
we learned
that two Starfleet officers

00:22:15.133 --> 00:22:17.328
were accused of murdering
the Klingon Chancellor.

00:22:17.368 --> 00:22:18.335
They were brought back

00:22:18.369 --> 00:22:20.132
to the Klingon Homeworld
to stand trial.

00:22:20.171 --> 00:22:23.402
Captain Sulu had served under
both officers for many years,

00:22:23.441 --> 00:22:25.500
and he felt
an intense loyalty to them.

00:22:27.745 --> 00:22:31.681
Helm, set a course
for Kronos, maximum warp.

00:22:31.716 --> 00:22:33.616
Take us through
the Azure Nebula.

00:22:33.651 --> 00:22:35.778
That should conceal
our approach.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:36.616
Aye, sir.

00:22:36.654 --> 00:22:37.643
I don't get it.

00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:38.986
What's going on?

00:22:39.057 --> 00:22:42.424
He's about to attempt a rescue
of Captain Kirk and Dr. McCoy.

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.623
As you can see, everyone
seemed perfectly willing

00:22:45.663 --> 00:22:47.324
to go along with this
breach of orders.

00:22:47.365 --> 00:22:49.697
However, I felt differently.

00:22:50.702 --> 00:22:53.000
Captain, am I correct
in assuming

00:22:53.071 --> 00:22:54.936
that you have decided to embark
on a rescue mission?

00:22:54.973 --> 00:22:55.997
That's right.

00:22:56.107 --> 00:22:58.268
Do you have a problem
with that, Ensign?

00:22:58.309 --> 00:22:59.367
I do.

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:01.207
It is a direct violation
of our orders

00:23:01.246 --> 00:23:03.373
from Starfleet Command,
and it could precipitate

00:23:03.414 --> 00:23:05.439
an armed conflict
between the Klingon Empire

00:23:05.483 --> 00:23:06.848
and the Federation.

00:23:06.884 --> 00:23:08.511
Objection noted.

00:23:08.553 --> 00:23:10.077
Resume your station.

00:23:10.121 --> 00:23:11.486
Sir, as a Starfleet officer,

00:23:11.522 --> 00:23:13.820
it is my duty
to formally protest.

00:23:13.858 --> 00:23:15.257
Tuvok...

00:23:15.293 --> 00:23:18.319
A pretty bold statement
for an Ensign

00:23:18.363 --> 00:23:22.231
with only... two months
space duty under his belt?

00:23:22.267 --> 00:23:24.326
I am aware
of my limited experience,

00:23:24.369 --> 00:23:27.361
but I am also very much aware
of Starfleet regulations

00:23:27.405 --> 00:23:29.339
and my obligation
to carry them out.

00:23:29.374 --> 00:23:31.239
That's enough.

00:23:31.276 --> 00:23:32.937
Ensign, you're relieved.

00:23:32.977 --> 00:23:35.172
I'm sorry about this, Captain.

00:23:35.213 --> 00:23:37.875
I assure you
it will not happen again.

00:23:37.915 --> 00:23:41.078
Ensign,
you're absolutely right,

00:23:41.119 --> 00:23:43.451
but you're also...

00:23:43.488 --> 00:23:45.388
absolutely wrong.

00:23:45.423 --> 00:23:47.084
You'll find that more happens

00:23:47.125 --> 00:23:48.786
on the Bridge of a starship
than just

00:23:48.826 --> 00:23:52.387
carrying out orders
and observing regulations.

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.364
There's a sense of loyalty

00:23:54.399 --> 00:23:57.163
to the men and women
you serve with...

00:23:57.201 --> 00:23:59.294
a sense of family.

00:23:59.337 --> 00:24:01.703
Those two men on trial...

00:24:01.739 --> 00:24:04.833
I served with them
for a long time.

00:24:04.876 --> 00:24:08.437
I owe them my life
a dozen times over,

00:24:08.479 --> 00:24:09.946
and right now,
they're in trouble

00:24:10.014 --> 00:24:11.811
and I'm going to help them.

00:24:11.849 --> 00:24:14.750
Let the regulations be damned.

00:24:14.786 --> 00:24:18.085
Sir, that is a most illogical
line of reasoning.

00:24:18.122 --> 00:24:20.181
You better believe it.

00:24:21.225 --> 00:24:23.125
Helm, engage.

00:24:25.663 --> 00:24:29.099
You know,
you did the right thing.

00:24:29.133 --> 00:24:31.968
Perhaps.

00:24:40.509 --> 00:24:43.672
Captain, we're approaching
the Azure Nebula.

00:24:43.713 --> 00:24:44.702
On screen.

00:24:51.287 --> 00:24:52.777
Tuvok...

00:24:54.991 --> 00:24:57.323
that nebula...

00:24:57.360 --> 00:25:00.852
it looks very similar to the one
we observed on Voyager.

00:25:03.032 --> 00:25:04.090
Help me, Tuvok!

00:25:05.434 --> 00:25:07.732
Please, don't let go!

00:25:07.770 --> 00:25:08.532
No!

00:25:11.807 --> 00:25:13.297
50 milligrams cordrazine.

00:25:18.314 --> 00:25:21.147
There was a sudden disruption
in his hippocampus.

00:25:21.183 --> 00:25:24.050
Luckily, he was in Sick Bay
or he'd be in a coma right now.

00:25:24.086 --> 00:25:25.576
That's the good news.

00:25:25.621 --> 00:25:27.748
The bad news is that
his synaptic pathways

00:25:27.790 --> 00:25:29.587
are continuing to degrade.

00:25:29.625 --> 00:25:31.593
If the repressed memory
keeps resurfacing

00:25:31.627 --> 00:25:33.322
on its own, it's going to
cause more and more damage.

00:25:33.362 --> 00:25:35.557
Eventually, his entire neural
structure will collapse,

00:25:35.598 --> 00:25:36.622
resulting in brain death.

00:25:36.665 --> 00:25:38.394
We were just starting
to make some progress.

00:25:38.434 --> 00:25:40.959
We finally accessed
the repressed memory.

00:25:41.070 --> 00:25:45.370
I saw Tuvok as a boy...

00:25:45.408 --> 00:25:46.932
and the girl on the precipice.

00:25:46.976 --> 00:25:48.773
Can I talk to him?

00:25:48.811 --> 00:25:49.835
Not yet.

00:25:49.879 --> 00:25:51.904
He suffered a severe
neural trauma,

00:25:51.947 --> 00:25:53.972
so I'm keeping him sedated
for the next few hours.

00:25:54.016 --> 00:25:56.109
I'll let you know when
it's safe to revive him.

00:26:09.565 --> 00:26:11.294
Come in.

00:26:11.333 --> 00:26:12.925
Ah, Ensign, what have you found?

00:26:13.002 --> 00:26:14.663
I don't see any connection
between this nebula

00:26:14.703 --> 00:26:16.933
and the one the Excelsior
saw 80 years ago.

00:26:17.006 --> 00:26:20.942
This one's a class-17,
while theirs was an 11.

00:26:21.010 --> 00:26:23.342
Both contained trace
amounts of sirillium,

00:26:23.379 --> 00:26:24.744
but that's about all.

00:26:24.780 --> 00:26:26.179
But they do look similar.

00:26:26.215 --> 00:26:28.945
To the naked eye,
but not to sensors.

00:26:28.984 --> 00:26:31.111
Technically,
they're very different.

00:26:31.153 --> 00:26:33.917
You know, I've been
talking to the Doctor,

00:26:33.956 --> 00:26:37.187
and he tells me it's not
unusual for a repressed memory

00:26:37.226 --> 00:26:40.855
to resurface because
of a smell or a visual detail.

00:26:40.896 --> 00:26:43.456
Maybe the visual similarities
between the two nebulas

00:26:43.499 --> 00:26:45.933
simply triggered Tuvok's
memory of the Excelsior.

00:26:45.968 --> 00:26:48.960
Well, what about the memory
of the little girl?

00:26:49.004 --> 00:26:51.097
What does she have to do
with Tuvok's experiences

00:26:51.140 --> 00:26:52.937
on board Sulu's ship?

00:26:52.975 --> 00:26:54.374
The Excelsior seemed

00:26:54.410 --> 00:26:56.970
so far removed from
that childhood incident.

00:26:57.012 --> 00:26:59.640
Who knows what goes on
in a Vulcan's mind?

00:26:59.682 --> 00:27:01.343
Maybe there is no connection

00:27:01.383 --> 00:27:03.476
and going back to the memory
of the Excelsior

00:27:03.519 --> 00:27:06.488
was just an accident, a stray
thought Tuvok was having

00:27:06.522 --> 00:27:08.581
because of the similarities
between the two nebulas.

00:27:08.624 --> 00:27:10.216
You may be right.

00:27:10.259 --> 00:27:13.126
Nevertheless, I've been
studying the Excelsior logs.

00:27:13.162 --> 00:27:15.255
What do they say?

00:27:15.297 --> 00:27:17.822
Unfortunately, they don't say
anything at all.

00:27:17.867 --> 00:27:18.925
Nothing?

00:27:19.034 --> 00:27:21.264
It would seem
that Captain Sulu decided

00:27:21.303 --> 00:27:24.067
not to enter that journey
into his official log.

00:27:24.106 --> 00:27:25.767
The day's entry makes
some cryptic remark

00:27:25.808 --> 00:27:28.038
about the ship being damaged
in a gaseous anomaly

00:27:28.077 --> 00:27:30.944
and needing repairs
but nothing else.

00:27:31.013 --> 00:27:33.243
You mean, he falsified his logs.

00:27:34.550 --> 00:27:36.814
It was a very different time,
Mr. Kim.

00:27:36.852 --> 00:27:39.650
Captain Sulu,
Captain Kirk, Dr. McCoy...

00:27:39.688 --> 00:27:41.383
they all belonged
to a different breed

00:27:41.423 --> 00:27:42.947
of Starfleet officer.

00:27:42.992 --> 00:27:44.892
Imagine the era they lived in...

00:27:44.927 --> 00:27:48.124
the Alpha Quadrant
still largely unexplored,

00:27:48.164 --> 00:27:50.530
humanity on verge
of war with Klingons,

00:27:50.566 --> 00:27:52.864
Romulans hiding
behind every nebula.

00:27:52.902 --> 00:27:54.631
Even the technology
we take for granted

00:27:54.670 --> 00:27:56.570
was still in its early stages.

00:27:56.605 --> 00:27:58.903
No plasma weapons,
no multiphasic shields.

00:27:58.941 --> 00:28:01.239
Their ships were half as fast.

00:28:01.277 --> 00:28:03.677
No replicators, no holodecks.

00:28:03.712 --> 00:28:05.145
You know, ever since I took

00:28:05.181 --> 00:28:07.274
Starfleet history
at the Academy,

00:28:07.316 --> 00:28:09.147
I always wondered
what it would be like

00:28:09.185 --> 00:28:11.153
to live in those days.

00:28:11.187 --> 00:28:14.645
Space must have seemed a
whole lot bigger back then.

00:28:16.158 --> 00:28:19.059
It's not surprising they had
to bend the rules a little.

00:28:19.094 --> 00:28:22.655
They were a little slower
to invoke the Prime Directive

00:28:22.698 --> 00:28:25.132
and a little quicker
to pull their phasers.

00:28:25.167 --> 00:28:26.361
Of course,
the whole bunch of them

00:28:26.402 --> 00:28:28.700
would be booted
out of Starfleet today,

00:28:28.737 --> 00:28:31.137
but I have to admit...

00:28:31.173 --> 00:28:33.801
I would have loved to ride
shotgun at least once

00:28:33.842 --> 00:28:35.742
with a group of officers
like that.

00:28:35.778 --> 00:28:37.336
Sick Bay to Captain Janeway.

00:28:37.379 --> 00:28:38.346
Go ahead, Doctor.

00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:40.348
I'm ready to revive Mr. Tuvok.

00:28:40.382 --> 00:28:41.349
Acknowledged.

00:28:41.383 --> 00:28:42.475
I'm on my way.

00:28:50.859 --> 00:28:52.884
Several hours
after we entered the nebula,

00:28:52.928 --> 00:28:54.919
we were ambushed by Klingons.

00:28:54.964 --> 00:28:56.955
A battle ensued,
and we were forced

00:28:57.032 --> 00:28:58.693
to abort our rescue mission.

00:28:58.734 --> 00:29:00.292
Do any of those events

00:29:00.336 --> 00:29:02.896
seem related to the girl
in any way?

00:29:02.972 --> 00:29:06.806
No. If there is a connection,
I am not aware of it.

00:29:06.842 --> 00:29:09.743
I suggest we attempt
another mind-meld

00:29:09.778 --> 00:29:12.576
and try again to access
my memory of the girl.

00:29:12.615 --> 00:29:13.206
Agreed.

00:29:13.249 --> 00:29:14.238
Doctor.

00:29:25.961 --> 00:29:28.691
Your mind to my mind.

00:29:28.731 --> 00:29:32.064
Your thoughts to my thoughts.

00:29:32.101 --> 00:29:34.763
I am taking us back...

00:29:34.803 --> 00:29:37.863
back to the boy that I was...

00:29:37.906 --> 00:29:40.466
the boy lying on the precipice.

00:29:41.944 --> 00:29:44.208
Hull breach on Deck 12,
Section 47.

00:29:44.246 --> 00:29:46.737
Tuvok, we're back in the battle

00:29:46.782 --> 00:29:49.114
with the Klingons again,
80 years ago.

00:29:49.151 --> 00:29:51.119
I am at a loss to explain,
Captain.

00:29:51.153 --> 00:29:53.314
But it's hard to accept
this as a coincidence.

00:29:53.355 --> 00:29:54.481
Agreed.

00:29:54.523 --> 00:29:57.924
I want to go back to the moment
when you first saw the nebula.

00:29:57.960 --> 00:29:59.222
What happened?

00:29:59.261 --> 00:30:02.822
Captain Sulu estimated it would
take approximately five hours

00:30:02.865 --> 00:30:05.356
to traverse the nebula
and enter Klingon space.

00:30:05.401 --> 00:30:08.199
He decided my shift
needed some rest,

00:30:08.237 --> 00:30:09.727
so we returned
to the crew quarters.

00:30:09.772 --> 00:30:11.433
I attempted to get some sleep.

00:30:11.473 --> 00:30:14.442
However, my bunkmate
Dmitri Valtane,

00:30:14.476 --> 00:30:16.307
felt the need to discuss
our situation.

00:30:16.345 --> 00:30:18.279
Hey.

00:30:18.314 --> 00:30:19.941
Tuvok.

00:30:19.982 --> 00:30:21.813
Are you asleep?

00:30:21.850 --> 00:30:22.976
No.

00:30:23.018 --> 00:30:24.212
Me neither.

00:30:24.253 --> 00:30:26.187
I can't believe
we're going to do this.

00:30:26.221 --> 00:30:28.519
I didn't think the Captain
had it in him.

00:30:28.557 --> 00:30:30.252
Had what in him?

00:30:30.292 --> 00:30:32.817
You know...
the guts to defy an order

00:30:32.861 --> 00:30:33.987
and run off
on some rescue mission

00:30:34.063 --> 00:30:35.690
to save old friends.

00:30:35.731 --> 00:30:37.790
I take it from the tone
of your voice,

00:30:37.833 --> 00:30:39.323
that you admire this trait.

00:30:39.368 --> 00:30:40.835
Well, yeah.

00:30:40.869 --> 00:30:42.393
It's courageous.

00:30:42.438 --> 00:30:43.996
It is illogical and reckless,

00:30:44.073 --> 00:30:46.098
which I attempted to point out
to him on the Bridge.

00:30:46.141 --> 00:30:48.268
Oh, come on, Tuvok.

00:30:48.310 --> 00:30:51.677
Isn't it more fun than
charting gaseous anomalies?

00:30:51.714 --> 00:30:55.115
The human fascination with fun
has led to many tragedies

00:30:55.150 --> 00:30:57.175
in your short
but violent history.

00:30:57.219 --> 00:30:58.743
One wonders
how your race has survived

00:30:58.787 --> 00:31:00.846
having so much fun.

00:31:00.889 --> 00:31:05.189
Ooh. Vulcans...
you guys need to relax.

00:31:05.227 --> 00:31:07.787
No. I will not relax.

00:31:07.830 --> 00:31:09.559
Ever since I entered
the Academy,

00:31:09.598 --> 00:31:12.362
I've had to endure the
egocentric nature of humanity.

00:31:12.401 --> 00:31:15.768
You believe that everyone in
the galaxy should be like you,

00:31:15.804 --> 00:31:17.897
that we should all share
your sense of humor

00:31:17.940 --> 00:31:19.567
and your human values.

00:31:19.608 --> 00:31:20.973
Well, if you hate it here
so much,

00:31:21.043 --> 00:31:23.944
why'd you join Starfleet
in the first place?

00:31:23.979 --> 00:31:25.708
I joined under pressure
from my parents,

00:31:25.748 --> 00:31:28.273
but I've already decided
to resign my commission

00:31:28.317 --> 00:31:30.376
once this assignment
is complete.

00:31:31.587 --> 00:31:34.021
Well, your loss.

00:31:38.861 --> 00:31:41.955
Tuvok, did you really mean that?

00:31:46.335 --> 00:31:49.463
At this point in my life, yes.

00:31:49.505 --> 00:31:51.439
My experiences at the Academy

00:31:51.473 --> 00:31:53.941
and on board the Excelsior
were not pleasant.

00:31:53.976 --> 00:31:55.238
I knew you left Starfleet

00:31:55.277 --> 00:31:57.370
for over 50 years,
but I never knew why.

00:31:57.413 --> 00:32:00.905
I didn't realize it was because
of a conflict with humans.

00:32:00.949 --> 00:32:03.884
My perceptions of humanity
and Starfleet

00:32:03.919 --> 00:32:05.580
were undoubtedly colored
by the fact

00:32:05.621 --> 00:32:07.418
that I did not want to be
here in the first place.

00:32:07.456 --> 00:32:10.050
Your parents really forced
you to go to the Academy?

00:32:10.092 --> 00:32:11.957
It was their wish

00:32:12.027 --> 00:32:14.325
and I felt an obligation
to fulfill it.

00:32:14.363 --> 00:32:17.560
What did you do
during those 50 years?

00:32:17.599 --> 00:32:19.328
I'd returned to Vulcan

00:32:19.368 --> 00:32:21.427
where I spent several years
in seclusion,

00:32:21.470 --> 00:32:23.529
immersing myself
in the Kolinahr...

00:32:23.572 --> 00:32:27.406
a rigorous discipline
intended to purge all emotions.

00:32:27.443 --> 00:32:30.344
I wanted to attain a state
of pure and total logic.

00:32:30.379 --> 00:32:31.846
What happened?

00:32:31.880 --> 00:32:33.905
Unfortunately,
six years into my studies,

00:32:33.949 --> 00:32:35.940
I began the Pon farr.

00:32:35.984 --> 00:32:37.451
I took a mate.

00:32:37.486 --> 00:32:38.453
T'Pel.

00:32:38.487 --> 00:32:41.650
Yes. We decided to raise
a family together.

00:32:41.690 --> 00:32:43.988
So I chose
to postpone my studies.

00:32:44.059 --> 00:32:46.459
And what brought you
back to Starfleet?

00:32:46.495 --> 00:32:49.362
Raising children of my own
made me appreciate

00:32:49.398 --> 00:32:52.595
what my parents
experienced raising me,

00:32:52.634 --> 00:32:54.124
and I came to realize

00:32:54.169 --> 00:32:56.000
that the decisions
I made as a young man

00:32:56.071 --> 00:32:58.403
were not always
in my best interest.

00:32:58.440 --> 00:33:01.739
I understood their decision
to send me to the Academy

00:33:01.777 --> 00:33:03.574
and that there were many things

00:33:03.612 --> 00:33:06.274
I could learn from humans
and other species.

00:33:06.315 --> 00:33:09.546
So I decided to expand
my knowledge of the galaxy.

00:33:09.585 --> 00:33:12.611
Starfleet provided
that opportunity.

00:33:12.654 --> 00:33:15.953
Well, I'm glad you
had a change of heart.

00:33:16.058 --> 00:33:17.958
As am I, Captain.

00:33:18.026 --> 00:33:20.961
Although, "heart" had
very little to do with it.

00:33:21.029 --> 00:33:22.690
It was a logical decision.

00:33:22.731 --> 00:33:24.130
I'm sure it was.

00:33:24.166 --> 00:33:25.394
Red Alert.

00:33:25.434 --> 00:33:27.402
All hands to battle stations.

00:33:27.436 --> 00:33:28.835
What's going on?

00:33:28.871 --> 00:33:30.930
I thought we were still
five hours from Klingon space.

00:33:30.973 --> 00:33:33.464
A Klingon battle cruiser
de-cloaked inside the nebula.

00:33:33.509 --> 00:33:35.374
At this moment, they were firing

00:33:35.410 --> 00:33:37.071
concussive charges
across our bow.

00:33:50.490 --> 00:33:51.855
We're being hailed, Captain.

00:33:51.892 --> 00:33:53.086
On screen.

00:33:53.126 --> 00:33:54.525
Mr. Sulu,

00:33:54.561 --> 00:33:58.588
I see they have finally given
you the Captaincy you deserve.

00:33:58.632 --> 00:34:00.293
Thank you, Kang.

00:34:00.333 --> 00:34:03.268
Do not let it end prematurely.

00:34:03.303 --> 00:34:06.739
Kang, we've been
on a survey mission

00:34:06.773 --> 00:34:08.365
studying this nebula.

00:34:08.408 --> 00:34:11.377
Our navigation system
malfunctioned

00:34:11.411 --> 00:34:14.073
and I'm afraid we got lost.

00:34:14.114 --> 00:34:16.309
As soon as we've
completed repairs,

00:34:16.349 --> 00:34:17.509
we'll be on our way.

00:34:17.551 --> 00:34:21.043
We'd be happy to escort you
back to Federation space.

00:34:21.088 --> 00:34:23.079
Very generous of you.

00:34:23.123 --> 00:34:24.488
But we can manage.

00:34:24.524 --> 00:34:26.822
I insist.

00:34:26.860 --> 00:34:30.523
Actually, an escort
would be welcome.

00:34:30.564 --> 00:34:32.896
We'd hate to lose our way again.

00:34:32.933 --> 00:34:36.960
Bring your ship about,
bearing 181 mark 2.

00:34:37.070 --> 00:34:39.595
Nice to see you again, Kang.

00:34:43.543 --> 00:34:44.703
Captain Sulu?

00:34:44.745 --> 00:34:46.076
Man your station, Lieutenant.

00:34:46.113 --> 00:34:48.206
We're not giving up just yet.

00:34:48.248 --> 00:34:49.909
Helm, come about.

00:34:59.526 --> 00:35:00.959
Tactical status.

00:35:00.994 --> 00:35:03.554
They have their forward
disruptors trained on us, sir.

00:35:05.532 --> 00:35:09.662
Ensign Tuvok, what is the
composition of this nebula?

00:35:09.703 --> 00:35:11.500
Primarily oxygen and argon

00:35:11.538 --> 00:35:14.632
with traces of theta-xenon,
fluorine and sirillium gas.

00:35:14.674 --> 00:35:17.199
Sirillium?

00:35:17.244 --> 00:35:19.542
That's a highly combustible
substance, isn't it?

00:35:19.579 --> 00:35:20.671
Affirmative.

00:35:20.714 --> 00:35:22.807
Is there any way we could
ignite the sirillium?

00:35:22.849 --> 00:35:24.043
If we modulated

00:35:24.084 --> 00:35:26.245
a positron beam
to a subspace frequency,

00:35:26.286 --> 00:35:28.584
it would trigger
a thermochemical reaction

00:35:28.622 --> 00:35:29.589
in the sirillium.

00:35:29.623 --> 00:35:32.820
Like tossing a match
into a pool of gasoline.

00:35:32.859 --> 00:35:35.851
Would their shields
withstand the blast?

00:35:35.896 --> 00:35:38.194
Yes. But their sensors
and tactical systems

00:35:38.231 --> 00:35:39.960
would be disrupted
for several seconds.

00:35:40.066 --> 00:35:41.897
That's all the time we need.

00:35:41.935 --> 00:35:45.393
Tuvok, modulate a positron beam
and stand by.

00:35:45.438 --> 00:35:48.703
We'll ignite the sirillium
the instant we clear the nebula.

00:35:48.742 --> 00:35:51.905
Helm, prepare to engage
maximum warp on my command.

00:35:51.945 --> 00:35:53.378
Aye, sir.

00:35:53.413 --> 00:35:55.108
All hands, this is the Captain.

00:35:55.148 --> 00:35:57.981
Secure stations
and batten down the hatches.

00:35:58.084 --> 00:36:00.609
The positron beam
is charged and ready.

00:36:00.654 --> 00:36:03.054
On my mark, Ensign.

00:36:03.089 --> 00:36:04.716
We're clearing the nebula.

00:36:04.758 --> 00:36:07.226
Mr. Tuvok, light the match.

00:36:17.237 --> 00:36:18.727
The Klingon ship's
been disabled.

00:36:18.772 --> 00:36:20.205
They're not pursuing, sir.

00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:23.801
Helm, set a course for Kronos.
Engage.

00:36:27.447 --> 00:36:29.813
Commander Rand, I want you...

00:36:29.850 --> 00:36:31.147
Sir, long-range sensors
are detecting

00:36:31.184 --> 00:36:33.118
three Klingon battle cruisers
on an intercept course.

00:36:33.153 --> 00:36:34.848
They're arming torpedoes.

00:36:36.489 --> 00:36:37.683
Heading, sir?

00:36:37.724 --> 00:36:39.157
Maintain course.

00:36:45.365 --> 00:36:46.957
Return fire!

00:36:47.067 --> 00:36:48.728
They've knocked out
our targeting scanners.

00:36:48.768 --> 00:36:50.599
Switch to manual!

00:36:52.072 --> 00:36:54.370
Mr. Valtane, there's a rupture

00:36:54.407 --> 00:36:56.341
in the plasma conduit
behind your console.

00:36:56.376 --> 00:36:57.206
Get away from that station!

00:36:57.244 --> 00:36:58.871
One more second.

00:36:58.912 --> 00:36:59.640
Dmitri, you must...

00:37:03.783 --> 00:37:06.445
Bridge to Sick Bay,
medical emergency!

00:37:09.990 --> 00:37:11.116
Tuvok...

00:37:16.463 --> 00:37:18.226
Tuvok!

00:37:18.932 --> 00:37:19.990
Help!

00:37:21.067 --> 00:37:22.694
Don't let me fall!

00:37:24.204 --> 00:37:25.637
No!

00:37:25.672 --> 00:37:28.607
Doctor, what's happening?

00:37:28.642 --> 00:37:30.769
Their memory engrams
are destabilizing.

00:37:30.810 --> 00:37:32.835
Something must be going
wrong with the mind-meld.

00:37:32.879 --> 00:37:35.541
I'm going to bring
them out of it.

00:37:39.719 --> 00:37:40.879
It's not working.

00:37:40.921 --> 00:37:43.355
Their neural patterns
appear to be locked together.

00:37:43.390 --> 00:37:44.857
I can't break the meld.

00:37:48.628 --> 00:37:50.721
The damage to his synaptic
patterns is accelerating.

00:37:50.764 --> 00:37:52.391
At this rate, he'll be
brain dead in 20 minutes.

00:37:52.432 --> 00:37:54.059
Get me a cortical stimulator!

00:37:54.100 --> 00:37:55.727
I saw her again, Tuvok...

00:37:55.769 --> 00:37:56.497
the girl.

00:37:56.536 --> 00:37:59.198
When Valtane died just now,

00:37:59.239 --> 00:38:01.469
it seemed to cause
the memory to resurface.

00:38:02.676 --> 00:38:03.802
What is it?

00:38:03.843 --> 00:38:06.004
Something's gone wrong
with the mind-meld.

00:38:06.046 --> 00:38:08.537
Who the hell are you?

00:38:12.786 --> 00:38:13.810
Intruder alert!

00:38:13.853 --> 00:38:14.877
Get security up here!

00:38:14.921 --> 00:38:16.479
What's happening?
Why can he see me?

00:38:16.523 --> 00:38:17.547
I asked you a question.

00:38:17.590 --> 00:38:19.649
Who are you and what are you
doing on my ship?

00:38:19.693 --> 00:38:21.786
It's an indication
that the rate of deterioration

00:38:21.828 --> 00:38:22.920
in my brain has increased.

00:38:22.996 --> 00:38:25.328
At advanced stages
of a t'Iokan schism,

00:38:25.365 --> 00:38:28.459
memories and thought processes
become distorted and confused.

00:38:28.501 --> 00:38:30.196
Ensign, do you know this woman?

00:38:30.236 --> 00:38:31.863
I will break the meld,
Captain.

00:38:31.905 --> 00:38:32.872
No, don't.

00:38:32.906 --> 00:38:34.396
I think we're getting
close to something.

00:38:34.441 --> 00:38:37.001
Everything seems to be centered
around the death of Valtane.

00:38:39.012 --> 00:38:42.209
Direct hit on the port bow.
Shields down to 20 percent.

00:38:42.248 --> 00:38:43.943
Losing atmosphere
on Decks 5, 6 and 7.

00:38:44.050 --> 00:38:47.281
I'll reroute auxiliary power
to structural integrity.

00:38:47.320 --> 00:38:49.345
Maybe something happened
in that moment

00:38:49.389 --> 00:38:50.686
between the two of you...

00:38:50.724 --> 00:38:52.521
some detail you
aren't remembering.

00:38:52.559 --> 00:38:55.426
I want you to try and replay
those events one more time.

00:38:55.462 --> 00:38:57.589
I will try,
but I must point out

00:38:57.630 --> 00:38:59.757
that if my neural structures
collapse during the meld,

00:38:59.799 --> 00:39:01.664
you will suffer
brain damage as well.

00:39:01.701 --> 00:39:03.532
I understand.

00:39:03.570 --> 00:39:05.663
Take those two to the brig.

00:39:05.705 --> 00:39:08.731
Captain, if we replay those
events and they see you,

00:39:08.775 --> 00:39:10.367
it will disrupt
the memory again.

00:39:10.410 --> 00:39:13.777
Then we've got to find a way
to make me inconspicuous.

00:39:17.083 --> 00:39:18.550
All right, Gamma Shift,

00:39:18.585 --> 00:39:22.214
time to defend the Federation
against gaseous anomalies.

00:39:23.289 --> 00:39:24.313
How are you, Ensign?

00:39:25.392 --> 00:39:26.654
Who are you?

00:39:29.996 --> 00:39:31.657
We could have just asked her.

00:39:31.698 --> 00:39:33.393
Asking female officers
for their clothing

00:39:33.433 --> 00:39:34.832
could lead to misunderstanding.

00:39:37.203 --> 00:39:38.693
I've programmed
a cortical stimulator

00:39:38.738 --> 00:39:40.933
to emit thoron radiation.

00:39:41.041 --> 00:39:43.339
We'll bombard
his telepathic cortex.

00:39:43.376 --> 00:39:45.901
That should be enough
to terminate the meld.

00:39:45.945 --> 00:39:47.469
We'll begin
with a 20-kilodyne burst

00:39:47.514 --> 00:39:49.539
of five-second duration
on my mark.

00:39:49.582 --> 00:39:51.311
Now.

00:39:52.485 --> 00:39:53.816
It's working.

00:39:53.853 --> 00:39:55.844
Their neural patterns
are starting to separate.

00:39:57.924 --> 00:39:59.050
My god.

00:39:59.092 --> 00:40:00.389
What is it?

00:40:00.427 --> 00:40:02.657
That's Tuvok's memory engram.

00:40:02.695 --> 00:40:03.719
That's the Captain's.

00:40:03.763 --> 00:40:06.095
But this red pattern
seems to be another engram.

00:40:06.132 --> 00:40:06.689
A third memory engram.

00:40:06.733 --> 00:40:07.825
How's that possible?

00:40:07.867 --> 00:40:08.891
It's not...

00:40:08.935 --> 00:40:10.596
which means it can't
really be an engram.

00:40:14.074 --> 00:40:15.507
From the neurochemical
modulation,

00:40:15.542 --> 00:40:17.669
I'd say it's something
masquerading as an engram.

00:40:17.710 --> 00:40:20.543
The way viruses sometimes mimic
certain blood factors to avoid

00:40:20.580 --> 00:40:22.172
being destroyed by antibodies?

00:40:22.215 --> 00:40:23.580
So you're saying it's a virus.

00:40:23.616 --> 00:40:24.810
I think so.

00:40:24.851 --> 00:40:26.318
The thoron radiation

00:40:26.352 --> 00:40:28.616
must have caused it
to manifest itself.

00:40:28.655 --> 00:40:31.920
Increasing the radiation level
should destroy it.

00:40:31.958 --> 00:40:33.983
Go to 40 kilodynes,
ten second burst.

00:40:34.027 --> 00:40:35.187
Now!

00:40:35.228 --> 00:40:37.594
The Klingon ship's
been disabled, sir.

00:40:37.630 --> 00:40:38.790
They're no longer pursuing.

00:40:38.832 --> 00:40:41.323
Helm, set a course for Kronos.

00:40:41.367 --> 00:40:42.356
Engage.

00:40:44.537 --> 00:40:46.528
Who's at communications?

00:40:46.573 --> 00:40:48.404
Commander Rand is supposed
to be on duty, sir.

00:40:48.441 --> 00:40:49.635
Where is she?

00:40:49.676 --> 00:40:50.904
Sir, long-range sensors

00:40:50.944 --> 00:40:52.775
are detecting three
Klingon battle cruisers

00:40:52.812 --> 00:40:54.575
on an intercept course.

00:40:54.614 --> 00:40:56.172
They're arming torpedoes.

00:40:56.216 --> 00:40:57.308
Maintain course.

00:40:59.252 --> 00:41:00.844
Return fire!

00:41:00.887 --> 00:41:02.752
They've knocked out
our targeting scanners, sir.

00:41:02.789 --> 00:41:03.949
Switch to manual.

00:41:06.559 --> 00:41:08.083
Mr. Valtane, there's a rupture

00:41:08.128 --> 00:41:10.358
in the plasma conduit
behind your console.

00:41:10.396 --> 00:41:11.727
Get away from that station.

00:41:11.764 --> 00:41:12.822
One more second.

00:41:12.866 --> 00:41:13.628
Dmitri, you must...

00:41:18.571 --> 00:41:20.129
It's about to happen.

00:41:20.173 --> 00:41:23.939
Try to remember every detail
about the next few seconds.

00:41:23.977 --> 00:41:25.205
Concentrate.

00:41:26.513 --> 00:41:27.810
Tuvok...

00:41:29.816 --> 00:41:31.875
Help me!

00:41:31.918 --> 00:41:32.976
Help me, Tuvok!

00:41:33.019 --> 00:41:34.418
I saw her, Tuvok.

00:41:34.454 --> 00:41:35.978
I saw the girl.

00:41:36.022 --> 00:41:37.046
Stay with it.

00:41:38.158 --> 00:41:39.284
I am trying.

00:41:39.325 --> 00:41:41.953
But my mind is weakening.

00:41:41.995 --> 00:41:43.986
This is our last chance.

00:41:44.063 --> 00:41:46.088
Take us to the precipice.

00:41:46.132 --> 00:41:47.394
Concentrate.

00:41:47.433 --> 00:41:49.424
Take us to the girl.

00:41:53.840 --> 00:41:54.829
It's working.

00:41:54.874 --> 00:41:55.966
The mind-meld is almost broken

00:41:56.009 --> 00:41:58.409
and the radiation appears
to be killing the virus.

00:41:58.444 --> 00:41:59.843
Increase thoron levels to...

00:42:01.915 --> 00:42:03.712
The virus is migrating.

00:42:03.750 --> 00:42:05.718
It's embedding itself
in the Captain's brain.

00:42:05.752 --> 00:42:06.946
Cortical stimulator.

00:42:08.621 --> 00:42:10.248
Kathryn!

00:42:10.290 --> 00:42:12.417
Help me, Kathryn, please!

00:42:12.458 --> 00:42:13.425
Don't let go.

00:42:13.459 --> 00:42:15.120
Don't let me fall!

00:42:16.728 --> 00:42:17.558
No!

00:42:17.596 --> 00:42:19.154
Program a 50-kilodyne burst

00:42:19.197 --> 00:42:21.529
five-second duration
on my mark. Now.

00:42:25.303 --> 00:42:26.531
Help me, Tuvok!

00:42:27.739 --> 00:42:29.934
The virus protein structures
are breaking down.

00:42:29.975 --> 00:42:31.101
It's dying.

00:42:31.142 --> 00:42:34.908
Increase thoron radiation
to 80 kilodynes 15 seconds. Now.

00:42:35.847 --> 00:42:37.280
Help me, Dmitri!

00:42:37.315 --> 00:42:38.282
Please, don't let go!

00:42:38.316 --> 00:42:39.544
Don't let me fall!

00:42:39.584 --> 00:42:40.608
Again!

00:42:40.652 --> 00:42:41.812
Don't let me fall!

00:42:41.853 --> 00:42:43.548
No!

00:42:44.222 --> 00:42:45.849
No!

00:42:46.424 --> 00:42:47.186
No!

00:42:47.959 --> 00:42:49.119
No!

00:42:50.462 --> 00:42:54.364
No!

00:43:08.079 --> 00:43:10.479
It's clearly a viral
parasite of some kind,

00:43:10.515 --> 00:43:12.847
but its origin
and genome classification

00:43:12.884 --> 00:43:14.146
are not on record.

00:43:14.185 --> 00:43:16.653
We were able to kill it
using thoron radiation.

00:43:16.688 --> 00:43:17.950
What do you know about it?

00:43:17.989 --> 00:43:21.481
The virus thrives on peptides
generated in the brain.

00:43:21.526 --> 00:43:22.959
It evades
the body's immune system

00:43:23.061 --> 00:43:25.586
by disguising itself
as a memory engram.

00:43:25.630 --> 00:43:27.393
Apparently, the parasite used

00:43:27.432 --> 00:43:30.333
the childhood memory of the
falling girl as camouflage.

00:43:30.368 --> 00:43:32.563
Creating a false memory
so traumatic

00:43:32.604 --> 00:43:35.072
that the mind would repress it
and that's where

00:43:35.106 --> 00:43:37.165
it would live,
in person after person,

00:43:37.208 --> 00:43:39.733
hiding in a part of the brain
that the conscious mind

00:43:39.778 --> 00:43:41.473
would want to avoid
at all costs.

00:43:41.513 --> 00:43:43.572
When it sensed
the death of the host,

00:43:43.615 --> 00:43:45.344
it would leave to find another.

00:43:45.383 --> 00:43:47.715
That's why it migrated
from Valtane to me.

00:43:47.752 --> 00:43:49.151
What about the girl?

00:43:49.187 --> 00:43:50.745
Did she ever really exist

00:43:50.789 --> 00:43:52.916
or did the organism
invent the memory?

00:43:52.957 --> 00:43:55.152
Memory is a tricky thing.

00:43:55.193 --> 00:43:58.287
If it was a real event,
it's been buried and copied

00:43:58.329 --> 00:43:59.762
and twisted so many times

00:43:59.798 --> 00:44:01.891
there's no way to tell
what really happened.

00:44:02.801 --> 00:44:03.825
Thank you, Doctor.

00:44:10.508 --> 00:44:11.873
I'm curious.

00:44:11.910 --> 00:44:14.435
Did the Excelsior ever
save Kirk and McCoy?

00:44:14.479 --> 00:44:15.741
Not directly.

00:44:15.780 --> 00:44:18.248
We were forced to retreat
back to Federation space.

00:44:18.283 --> 00:44:22.117
As usual, Captain Kirk provided
his own means of escape.

00:44:22.153 --> 00:44:23.848
But we did play a pivotal role

00:44:23.888 --> 00:44:25.583
at the subsequent battle
at Khitomer.

00:44:25.623 --> 00:44:28.524
Mr. Tuvok, if I didn't
know you better,

00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:30.755
I'd say you miss
those days on the Excelsior.

00:44:30.795 --> 00:44:32.194
On the contrary.

00:44:32.230 --> 00:44:34.960
I do not experience
feelings of nostalgia.

00:44:35.066 --> 00:44:37.728
But there are times when I
think back to those days

00:44:37.769 --> 00:44:40.966
of meeting Kirk, Spock
and the others,

00:44:41.072 --> 00:44:43.199
and I am pleased
that I was part of it.

00:44:43.241 --> 00:44:44.640
In a funny way,

00:44:44.676 --> 00:44:47.304
I feel like I was
a part of it, too.

00:44:47.345 --> 00:44:50.746
Then perhaps you can be
nostalgic for both of us.
